<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The Developer ID build's entitlements: .github/workflows/build.yml signs the macOS app with them (hardened runtime),
under team G88U5B5783.

- application-identifier, team-identifier, keychain-access-groups: KeychainSecretStore keeps the account's secrets in
  the data protection keychain, which on macOS needs the app's access group. These are restricted entitlements, so the
  app must carry a Developer ID provisioning profile for com.edde746.tortuga that grants them
  (Contents/embedded.provisionprofile, from the MACOS_PROVISIONING_PROFILE_BASE64 secret); without one macOS refuses
  to launch the app.
- associated-domains: a title's link (https://usetortuga.app/t/…, which Detail's Share sends) opens the app as a
  Universal Link, the site's /.well-known/apple-app-site-association naming this App ID. Also restricted: the
  Developer ID profile must grant it (the App ID's Associated Domains capability), or macOS refuses to launch the app.
- allow-jit, allow-unsigned-executable-memory: the exceptions for the embedded MPVKit (LuaJIT).
- No App Sandbox.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.application-identifier</key>
	<string>G88U5B5783.com.edde746.tortuga</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.team-identifier</key>
	<string>G88U5B5783</string>
	<key>keychain-access-groups</key>
	<array>
		<string>G88U5B5783.com.edde746.tortuga</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.associated-domains</key>
	<array>
		<string>applinks:usetortuga.app</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
